{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-09-16 15:23:03 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-16 22:23:03 +07 (Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh)\n\nRevised only [docs/design/dao.jing.cbor.md](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.jing.cbor.md). Preserved its section skeleton, design-contract altitude, and unchanged implementation status.\n\nChanges by section:\n\n- **Community precedent:** Added verified sources, Konserve’s BETA qualification, byte-stability ownership, and explicit encoder-option requirements (**P3-9**).\n- **Layering and interfaces:** Assigned address verification to the wrapper and untrusted-put verification to receiving backends (**P3-7**). Restricted canonical re-encoding to ingress while retaining hash verification on every retrieval (**P3-6; unresolved decision 3**). Added the architect’s effect-stream compatibility sentence.\n- **Encoding contract:** Required unpaired-surrogate rejection (**P2-2**). Chose named frames for **all identifiers**, eliminating the ambiguous native/escaped predicate (**unresolved decision 2**). Pinned tagged-literal writes and closed UnknownRecord conversion, with explicit TaggedValue/SimpleValue rejection.\n- **Numeric identity:** Defined numeric equality, hashing, ordering, native/carrier interoperability, and obligations for B-tree ordering and query matching (**P2-1; unresolved decision 1**). Preserved rich numeric kinds and integer/float address separation; explicitly prohibited native CBOR floats.\n- **Memory and files:** Replaced frame addresses with raw 32-byte digests and specified replay validation (**P3-4**).\n- **Remote and DHT:** Specified the 1200-byte budget, Base64 arithmetic, local-only oversized degradation, and the decision to add no WebSocket byte cap (**P3-5**). Required coordinated upgrades and loud mixed-version failures, including valid-Base64 legacy-string handling (**P3-8**).\n- **Addressing and clean break:** Defined nondestructive format recognition and tail recovery, including rejection of an unrecognizable interrupted first frame.\n- **Validation:** Added every requested scenario and explicit injectivity acceptance alongside byte identity and round-trip stability (**P2-3**), plus ingress-validation, extension-frame, and transport-boundary checks.\n\nAll findings and decisions were incorporated. No new upstream claims outside the supplied evidence were introduced. Option/profile precedence and Boring’s surrogate pre-validation remain explicitly **unverified**; Jing’s contract does not depend on either.\n\nDocument checks passed for section preservation, status, code fences, whitespace, and requirement coverage. No implementation tests were run because this was documentation-only work.\n\nOther documents need follow-up during implementation, but were not edited:\n\n- `dao.jing.md`: replace transitional encoding and superseded limitations.\n- `dao.jing.dht.md`: document byte transport, ingress checks, and effective payload budgets.\n- B-tree/query design references: document portable numeric comparison and matching.\n- Downstream address documentation: record fixture regeneration and coordinated rebuilding."}}
